fin-strategy:CalculationContext a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "Calculation Context, is a versioned calculation context that fixes the metric calculation frequency, annualization, risk-free rate, window, confidence, and result-affecting policies, used for freezing the complete parameter policy as an immutable snapshot to enable reproducible performance comparison. The market calendar, time zone, session anchor, maximum staleness, and fill-value marking are exposed as a queryable CalendarAnchoringPolicy rather than a hard-coded universal axiom, and the benchmark is expressed via a versioned BenchmarkSpecification.";
